[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: GHOST Model Context Protocol Requirements
UID: GHOST-MCP
VERSION: 0.1-draft
OPTIONS:
  MARKUP: Text
  AUTO_LEVELS: On
  NODE_IN_TOC: True

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 1. Purpose and Scope

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This document defines the parent requirements for the GHOST Model Context Protocol capability.

MCP is a first-class GHOST interface family. It is not part of the graphical/human-interface requirement family.

This document owns the common MCP contract shared by all GHOST MCP capabilities:
- protocol and transport;
- client interoperability;
- authentication and authorization;
- authenticated owner identity;
- tool discovery and invocation;
- request isolation;
- rate limiting;
- common error and security behavior;
- deployment ownership boundaries; and
- capability-extension governance.

Detailed functional behavior is owned by the MCP child requirement files:

- 111_mcp_capabilities.sdoc:
  Prompt Engineering, Episodic Memory, Clipboard Memory, and Collection Memory.

- 112_mcp_activeblackboard.sdoc:
  all current and future ActiveBlackboard behavior, including the current Persistent Chat prototype.

Runtime, container, local-hosting, AWS, reverse-proxy, HTTPS, Cognito, and deployment realization remain owned by the Runtime Platform and Operations requirement family.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-ROOT
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: GHOST MCP Capability Scope
STATEMENT: >>>
GHOST shall provide a Model Context Protocol interface through which approved external AI clients can invoke explicitly exposed GHOST capabilities.

The MCP capability shall provide a controlled external boundary around approved GHOST functions without transferring ownership of those functions to the MCP transport layer.

MCP shall be represented as its own capability family in the GHOST requirement hierarchy.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-SRS-FILE-TREE

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-CHILD-DOCUMENTS
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: MCP Child Requirement Documents
STATEMENT: >>>
The MCP capability shall be decomposed into:

1. 111_mcp_capabilities.sdoc for all approved MCP capabilities except ActiveBlackboard.
2. 112_mcp_activeblackboard.sdoc for all current and future ActiveBlackboard behavior.

The child files shall inherit from GHOST-MCP-ROOT and shall not duplicate the common protocol, authorization, transport, deployment-boundary, or client-interoperability requirements owned by this document.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-ROOT

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-INTERFACE-OWNERSHIP
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: MCP Interface Ownership
STATEMENT: >>>
The MCP parent capability shall own:

- external MCP protocol behavior;
- MCP transport requirements;
- MCP capability negotiation;
- tool discovery and invocation rules;
- authenticated caller identity;
- authorization enforcement;
- common tool-call rate limiting;
- interface-visible errors;
- cross-client interoperability;
- shared MCP security boundaries; and
- the boundary between MCP functionality and runtime/deployment realization.

The MCP parent capability shall not duplicate the internal algorithms of Prompt Engineering, Memory Management, ActiveBlackboard, or other GHOST functional subsystems.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-ROOT

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-PRODUCT-PACKAGE-BOUNDARY
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Product and Python Package Naming Boundary
STATEMENT: >>>
The product exposed through MCP shall be named GHOST.

The existing Python package namespace may remain ragstream in implementation paths.

MCP tool descriptions and client-facing metadata shall not present RAGstream as the product identity.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-ROOT

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 2. MCP Communication Contract

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-REMOTE-TOOL-PROVIDER
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: MCP Tool Provider Role
STATEMENT: >>>
The GHOST MCP server shall act as a tool provider.

An external AI client shall explicitly invoke an exposed GHOST MCP operation.

The MCP server shall not claim to passively receive, monitor, intercept, or persist ordinary client conversation traffic for which no applicable GHOST tool invocation occurs.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-ROOT

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-CLIENT-COMPATIBILITY
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: ChatGPT and Claude Compatibility
STATEMENT: >>>
The same GHOST MCP service contract shall be usable by approved ChatGPT and Claude MCP client integrations.

Core GHOST semantics shall not change merely because the invoking client is ChatGPT rather than Claude.

Client-specific user-interface behavior, connector configuration, or authentication setup may differ without creating different GHOST functional contracts.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-ROOT

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-EXPLICIT-CLIENT-INVOCATION
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Explicit Client Invocation Boundary
STATEMENT: >>>
A GHOST MCP operation shall execute only when the client issues the corresponding MCP request.

Enabling a GHOST connector or plugin shall not by itself authorize GHOST to treat every ordinary client message as an MCP operation.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-CLIENT-COMPATIBILITY

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-REMOTE-STREAMABLE-HTTP
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Streamable HTTP Transport
STATEMENT: >>>
The remote GHOST MCP service shall support MCP through Streamable HTTP.

The server shall provide a logical MCP endpoint supporting the protocol operations required by the selected MCP implementation.

Concrete hostnames, ports, reverse-proxy rules, container topology, and AWS network realization shall remain owned by the Runtime Platform and Operations requirement family.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-ROOT

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-EXTERNAL-HTTPS
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Protected External HTTPS
STATEMENT: >>>
Remote MCP clients shall communicate with the deployed GHOST MCP endpoint through HTTPS.

External clients shall not be required to connect directly to an unencrypted public application port or directly to an internal container port.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-REMOTE-STREAMABLE-HTTP

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-PROTOCOL-INITIALIZATION
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: MCP Initialization and Capability Negotiation
STATEMENT: >>>
The GHOST MCP server shall support the MCP initialization exchange and shall advertise only protocol capabilities supported by the active server implementation.

The server shall advertise tool capability when GHOST tools are available.

Additional MCP protocol capabilities shall not be claimed merely because they exist in the MCP specification or client implementation.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-REMOTE-STREAMABLE-HTTP

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-TOOLS-LIST
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Tool Discovery
STATEMENT: >>>
tools/list shall return the GHOST MCP tools currently approved and exposed by the active server implementation.

Tool discovery shall be the authoritative client-visible inventory of callable GHOST MCP operations.

An implementation experiment shall not automatically become a permanent GHOST requirement merely because it temporarily appears in tool metadata or code.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-PROTOCOL-INITIALIZATION

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-TOOLS-CALL
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Tool Invocation
STATEMENT: >>>
The server shall accept tools/call only for an advertised and authorized GHOST tool.

Before application behavior executes, the request shall pass applicable:
- protocol validation;
- authentication;
- authorization;
- rate limiting; and
- tool-input validation.

An unknown or undeclared tool shall not invoke GHOST application logic.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-TOOLS-LIST

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 3. Authentication, Authorization, and Owner Isolation

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-PROTECTED-ACCESS
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Protected MCP Access
STATEMENT: >>>
The deployed remote MCP service shall require authenticated access through the approved MCP-compatible OAuth authorization flow.

An unauthenticated or invalidly authenticated remote request shall not execute a protected GHOST tool.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-ROOT

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-OAUTH-PROTECTED-RESOURCE-METADATA
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: OAuth Protected Resource Metadata
STATEMENT: >>>
The protected remote GHOST MCP endpoint shall expose the OAuth Protected Resource Metadata required by the supported client connection flow.

The metadata shall identify the canonical GHOST MCP resource and the approved authorization server.

Concrete authorization-provider deployment details remain owned by the deployment requirements.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-PROTECTED-ACCESS

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-BEARER-TOKEN-TRANSPORT
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Bearer Token Transport
STATEMENT: >>>
An authenticated MCP client shall present its access token through the HTTP Authorization header using the Bearer scheme.

Access tokens shall not be accepted through URI query parameters.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-PROTECTED-ACCESS

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-TOKEN-RESOURCE-VALIDATION
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Token Validation
STATEMENT: >>>
Before executing a protected MCP operation, GHOST shall validate the presented token according to the active authorization configuration, including expiration and resource/scope requirements where applicable.

A token that does not authorize the GHOST MCP resource shall not authorize a GHOST tool call.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-PROTECTED-ACCESS

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-OWNER-ISOLATION
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Authenticated Owner Isolation
STATEMENT: >>>
Where an MCP capability accesses persistent user-owned state, the authenticated identity shall define the owner scope for that operation.

The current MCP memory implementation uses the authenticated Cognito subject as owner_sub.

A memory lookup, list, append, resume, or deletion operation shall not expose or mutate another authenticated owner's persistent data.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-PROTECTED-ACCESS

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-AUTHENTICATION-FAILURE
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Authentication Failure Response
STATEMENT: >>>
A protected request without valid authentication shall fail before application-tool execution.

The failure response shall not reveal access tokens, secrets, internal stack traces, stored memory bodies, prompt contents, or other protected GHOST state.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-PROTECTED-ACCESS

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-AUTHORIZATION-FAILURE
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Authorization Failure Response
STATEMENT: >>>
An authenticated request that lacks authorization for the requested MCP operation shall be rejected without executing the tool.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-PROTECTED-ACCESS

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-ORIGIN-VALIDATION
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Streamable HTTP Origin Validation
STATEMENT: >>>
The remote MCP runtime shall apply the configured transport-security policy, including Origin validation where required by the selected MCP transport implementation.

Accepted hosts and origins are deployment values and shall remain outside the functional MCP capability requirements.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-REMOTE-STREAMABLE-HTTP

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 4. Shared Runtime and Safety Behavior

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-TOOL-RATE-LIMITING
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Authenticated Tool Rate Limiting
STATEMENT: >>>
Authenticated GHOST MCP tool invocations shall be subject to configurable rate limiting before the protected application operation executes.

The current runtime identifies callers by authenticated owner identity.

Concrete quotas, time windows, and deployment values shall remain deployment configuration rather than fixed functional requirements.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-TOOLS-CALL

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-REQUEST-ISOLATION
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Request Isolation
STATEMENT: >>>
Concurrent MCP calls shall not accidentally exchange request-specific mutable state or tool results.

Persistent state may be shared only through an explicitly defined persistent capability such as memory or ActiveBlackboard and only according to its owning requirements.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-TOOLS-CALL

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-MALFORMED-REQUEST-ERROR
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Malformed MCP Request Error
STATEMENT: >>>
Malformed MCP or JSON-RPC requests, unsupported protocol operations, and unknown tool identifiers shall be rejected through the applicable MCP error path before GHOST application functionality executes.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-ROOT

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-ERROR-SANITIZATION
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Error Information Sanitization
STATEMENT: >>>
Client-visible MCP failures shall provide sufficient information to identify the failed operation without exposing:

- secrets;
- bearer tokens;
- provider credentials;
- hidden reasoning;
- internal prompts not intended for output;
- raw internal model responses;
- stack traces;
- protected filesystem details; or
- another owner's persistent data.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-MALFORMED-REQUEST-ERROR

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-TOOL-METADATA-TRUTH
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Tool Metadata Shall Match Behavior
STATEMENT: >>>
MCP tool metadata, including read-only, destructive, persistence, and idempotency indications, shall reflect the actual approved behavior of the corresponding operation.

A destructive or persistent operation shall not be presented to the client as harmless or read-only.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-TOOLS-LIST

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 5. Functional Ownership Boundaries

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-PREPROCESSING-OWNERSHIP-REFERENCE
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Prompt Processing Ownership Boundary
STATEMENT: >>>
The existing GHOST Prompt Engineering capability shall reuse the owning PreProcessing, PromptShaper, Agent Stack, SuperPrompt, and projection behavior rather than implementing duplicate prompt-processing algorithms inside the MCP transport layer.

Detailed Prompt Engineering MCP behavior is owned by 111_mcp_capabilities.sdoc.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-INTERFACE-OWNERSHIP

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-AWS-OWNERSHIP-REFERENCE
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Runtime and Deployment Ownership Boundary
STATEMENT: >>>
Runtime Platform and Operations requirements shall remain responsible for:

- local runtime realization;
- AWS runtime realization;
- container execution;
- image delivery;
- public endpoint realization;
- HTTPS termination;
- reverse proxy;
- DNS;
- authorization-provider deployment;
- secrets delivery;
- process startup and restart;
- persistent deployment paths; and
- operational verification.

This MCP requirement family shall define what the MCP capability must do, while the 80-series requirement family shall define how the supported runtime environments deploy and operate it.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-INTERFACE-OWNERSHIP

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-UI-OWNERSHIP-BOUNDARY
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Human Interface Boundary
STATEMENT: >>>
The MCP service shall not own the native ChatGPT or Claude user interface.

The Streamlit and future React/FastAPI interfaces remain separate GHOST interface capabilities.

An MCP result may be rendered by the invoking client without transferring ownership of the native client UI to GHOST.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-INTERFACE-OWNERSHIP

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-MEMORY-OWNERSHIP-BOUNDARY
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Memory Infrastructure Ownership Boundary
STATEMENT: >>>
MCP memory capabilities may use the common GHOST MemoryRecord, .ragmem, .ragmeta.json, SQLite, vector, and memory-management infrastructure.

The MCP capability requirements shall define MCP-specific memory semantics without redefining unrelated GUI memory-pipeline behavior.

Where existing Memory Management requirements remain applicable, they shall remain authoritative for their existing scope.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-INTERFACE-OWNERSHIP

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 6. Client and Protocol Acceptance

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-PROTOCOL-ACCEPTANCE
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: MCP Protocol Acceptance
STATEMENT: >>>
The MCP runtime shall be testable through a complete protocol sequence including:

1. initialize;
2. initialized notification where required;
3. tools/list; and
4. tools/call for an advertised tool.

The result shall conform to the declared MCP contract of the selected tool.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-ROOT

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-CHATGPT-ACCEPTANCE
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: ChatGPT End-to-End Acceptance
STATEMENT: >>>
A deployed GHOST MCP capability intended for ChatGPT shall be verified with the real supported ChatGPT client connection flow.

Successful local unit testing alone shall not be treated as proof of ChatGPT interoperability.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-PROTOCOL-ACCEPTANCE

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-CLAUDE-ACCEPTANCE
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Claude End-to-End Acceptance
STATEMENT: >>>
A deployed GHOST MCP capability intended for Claude shall be verified with the real supported Claude client connection flow.

Successful local unit testing alone shall not be treated as proof of Claude interoperability.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-PROTOCOL-ACCEPTANCE

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-CROSS-CLIENT-CONSISTENCY
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Cross-Client Functional Consistency
STATEMENT: >>>
ChatGPT and Claude shall invoke the same underlying GHOST capability semantics when they call the same MCP tool.

Client-specific presentation or connection details shall not create different persistence, retrieval, deletion, or prompt-engineering semantics.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-CLIENT-COMPATIBILITY

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 7. Controlled Extension and Requirement Stability

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The former 73_mcp_interface.sdoc described an earlier, prompt-engineering-only MCP scope.

Requirements from that document whose engineering meaning remains valid retain their established GHOST-MCP requirement UIDs in this new MCP family.

Obsolete single-tool exclusions are not reused for a different meaning.

New MCP functionality receives new UIDs rather than silently redefining unrelated existing requirements.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-EXTENSION-APPROVAL
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Explicit Approval for MCP Scope Extension
STATEMENT: >>>
A new MCP capability shall be added only through explicitly approved requirements defining the behavior necessary for that capability.

The presence of experimental implementation code shall not by itself promote that experiment to a permanent product requirement.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-ROOT

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GHOST-MCP-CONTRACT-CHANGE-CONTROL
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: MCP Contract Change Control
STATEMENT: >>>
A material change to an approved MCP tool identifier, required input, output semantics, persistence effects, destructive behavior, authorization boundary, or retrieval behavior shall be treated as an MCP interface-contract change.

The change shall be reflected in approved requirements and corresponding verification before it is treated as the new stable contract.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GHOST-MCP-EXTENSION-APPROVAL

[[/SECTION]]
